To fix this, the application must perform the blocklist check immediately before every connection attempt, not just at setup. The best approach is to use a custom network 'dialer' that resolves the hostname to an IP and checks that IP against the blocklist every single time a connection is opened. In Gitea, the fix involved ensuring the 'git push' command respects the same security policies as the 'LFS' and 'Pull' mirror components.

// Example of a safer check logic:
func safeSync(url string) {
    ip := resolveDNS(url)
    if isBlocklisted(ip) {
        return error("Forbidden destination")
    }
    performPush(ip) // Connect directly to the verified IP
}
